In this strategy, designers should consider not just the product, but also the material used to make it, as well as where the material origin from and where it may be discarded. Designers frequently overlook this strategy, but material and production choices can have a direct impact on entire communities.

Designers must consider three interwoven aspects of the production process: 
- ecological security; 
- resource security; 
- and socioeconomic security.

This strategy frequently conflicts with the maximisation of human and ecological resources in a specified area.